{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA1496462","title":"Studies of antibiotic resistance genes and microbial community in rainbow trout aquaculture effluents","description":"Rainbow trout have stringent water quality requirements during culture, and recirculating aquaculture systems are being increasingly adopted for intensive rainbow trout farming. However, whether improved conventional effluent quality is accompanied by a reduced antibiotic resistance gene (ARG) burden remains unclear.In this study, Effluents were collected from four RAS farms and four paved flow-through raceway systems (PFRS). Water quality parameters, including total nitrogen (TN), total phosphorus (TP), chemical oxygen demand (COD), chlorophyll-a (Chl-a), and dissolved oxygen (DO), were measured. Microbial community composition was characterized using 16S rRNA gene sequencing.This study demonstrates that conventional water-quality indicators alone are insufficient to evaluate resistance-associated genetic pollution in engineered aquaculture systems, and that ARGs, MGEs, microbial community structure, and species-ARG association patterns should be integrated into future rainbow trout aquaculture monitoring and management.","center":"Beijing Academy of Agriculture and Forestry Sciences","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2026/07/16 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN61718763","MIMARKS Survey related sample from fish metagenome","non_environmental",null,"2026-05-25",2026,"CN","Jilin",2038584,"Baishan","probable",41.8,127.0,"China: Baishan",null,"aquatic biome [ENVO:00000447]","aquaculture facility [ENVO:01000840]‌","waste water [ENVO:00002001]","host-derived or clinical material"],["SAMN61718764","MIMARKS Survey related sample from fish metag